# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
# ...and the symlink of the same name. `/.next/` with a trailing slash
# matches a directory only, so once `.next` became a link to
# `.next.nosync` git started offering to commit it.
/.next
/out/
# The real build directory. `.next` is a symlink to it.
#
# This tree lives under ~/Documents, which is synced by iCloud Drive, and a
# Next build writes tens of thousands of small files into `.next`. iCloud tries
# to sync them mid-build, which corrupts the output: routes start 500ing with
# "Cannot find module './NNNN.js'", the CSS asset 404s, and conflict
# directories named "cache 2" appear inside `.next`. A single `rm -rf .next`
# took over eight minutes because every file had to be materialised first.
#
# macOS excludes any path ending in `.nosync` from iCloud, so the build output
# goes there and `.next` points at it. Delete both if you ever move this repo
# out of a synced folder.
/.next.nosync/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

